-- title:
--   Degree-zero chart divisors force unit reductions at the nodes
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, $\pi \in A$ a nonzero element of the maximal ideal, and $F$ a field extension of $L$. Let $\bar F_0,\dots,\bar F_{n-1}$ be fields over the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$ in which every nonzero element admits a finitely supported divisor recording its orders at all places and of degree $0$, and in which every place is rational (the residue field of each place is generated by $\kappa$). For each $i$ let $C_i$ be a component chart of $F$ along $A$ with values in $\bar F_i$, all places in the domain of $C_i$ being rational. Let $An_e, An'_e$ ($e < m$) be annuli in $F$ over $A$, with source and target maps $\mathrm{src},\mathrm{tgt} \colon \{0,\dots,m-1\} \to \{0,\dots,n-1\}$, places $xs_e$ of $\bar F_{\mathrm{src}(e)}$ and $xt_e$ of $\bar F_{\mathrm{tgt}(e)}$, and weights $w_e \in \mathbb{N}$, subject to: $An'_e$ has the same domain and the same modulus as $An_e$, that modulus is nonzero in $L$ and equals the product of the two parameters; the modulus of $An_e$ is a unit of $A$ times $\pi^{w_e}$; $An_e$ is attached to $C_{\mathrm{src}(e)}$ at the node $xs_e$ and $An'_e$ to $C_{\mathrm{tgt}(e)}$ at the node $xt_e$ (so each is a node of the respective chart, the annulus parameter lies in the chart's ring of integers with reduction of order $1$ at the node, and the unit estimate of `IsAttached` holds); and every node of every chart occurs as an end $xs_e$ or $xt_e$ of exactly one annulus, in the sense that the map from two copies of the edge set to pairs (chart index, place) given by $e \mapsto (\mathrm{src}(e),xs_e)$ and $e \mapsto (\mathrm{tgt}(e),xt_e)$ hits each node and is injective over it. Then for every nonzero $f \in F$ with $\operatorname{ord}_P f = 0$ at every place $P$ in every annulus domain, and every family of divisors $E_i$ on $F/L$ with $E_i(P) = \operatorname{ord}_P f$ for $P$ in the domain of $C_i$, $E_i(P) = 0$ outside it, and $\deg E_i = 0$ for all $i$, there are nonzero constants $c_i \in L$ such that: each $c_i f$ lies in the ring of integers of $C_i$ with nonzero reduction, and that reduction has order $0$ at every node of $C_i$; for each $e$ the valuations of $c_{\mathrm{src}(e)}$ and $c_{\mathrm{tgt}(e)}$ in $A$ coincide; and for each $e$ and each place $P$ in the domain of $An_e$, the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(c_{\mathrm{src}(e)} f)$ lies in $A$ and is a unit there.
--
--   This is the degree-zero form of the statement that a function with no zeros or poles on the annuli of a semistable covering has vanishing slope along every annulus: the chart degrees being zero, harmonicity of the slope function on the dual graph (via [`WeightedMultigraph.slope_eq_zero_of_gradient_of_harmonic`](thm.html#WeightedMultigraph.slope_eq_zero_of_gradient_of_harmonic)) forces all slopes to vanish, so that a single constant per component makes $f$ a unit with reduction of order zero at the nodes. It feeds the bound for chart-supported principal divisors in a semistable model, [`AlgebraicCurve.le_add_one_and_exists_finset_card_le_pow_of_chartSupported_principal_of_semistableCovering_of_discFibres_of_rankOne_of_charZero_of_semistableModel`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.le_add_one_and_exists_finset_card_le_pow_of_chartSupported_principal_of_semistableCovering_of_discFibres_of_rankOne_of_charZero_of_semistableModel), and thus the well-definedness of periods of toric divisor classes.
